const faqs: [string, string][] = [["How much does an AI receptionist cost in Australia?", "Provider published AI receptionist plans in Australia run from about $44 to $899 per month. Entry tiers suit low call volumes with capped minutes, while upper tiers add longer call handling, integrations and custom voices. Effective per call cost falls as volume grows because there is no extra staffing."], ["How much does a human virtual receptionist cost in Australia?", "Human virtual receptionist plans typically start around $250 per month and reach $700 or more, depending on included minutes, after hours cover and dedicated receptionist arrangements. Unlike AI pricing, human costs scale with call minutes, so busy months cost noticeably more than quiet ones."], ["Can an AI receptionist handle Australian accents?", "Most modern AI receptionists are trained on Australian speech and manage everyday accents well, though strong accents, background noise or emotionally charged calls can still cause misunderstandings. Test with real callers before committing, and consider human handling for complex or distressed callers."], ["Is an AI receptionist compliant with the Privacy Act?", "Compliance depends on the vendor's data practices, not just the software. Ask for their privacy policy, data processing terms, recording and transcript retention periods and hosting location before signing. Under the Australian Privacy Act 1988, your business stays responsible for how personal information collected on calls is handled."], ["Can I combine an AI receptionist with human receptionists?", "Yes. Hybrid models let AI answer routine calls, overflow and after hours while humans take complex, sensitive or high value calls. Common patterns include AI screening with warm transfer to a person, and AI covering nights and weekends while humans run business hours."], ["Which should a small Australian business choose first?", "Start with an AI trial if most calls are routine bookings, price questions and after hours enquiries: the $44 entry point sits far below the human $250 floor. Choose human receptionists first if callers need judgment, empathy or complex scheduling. A hybrid upgrade covers both."]];

